# Netlify reads this file. A rule without "!" never shadows a file that exists,
# so every page of this site is served as itself and only an address the site
# does not have falls through to the last line.
#
# The domain of this site used to serve the hosted application, and people hold
# links to it: a document somebody was sent, a client page, a timesheet. None of
# them is a page here, so each is handed to the application, path and query
# kept, rather than answered with a 404.
#
# The comparison of two countries used to be a page per pair, /compare/<a>-<b>/,
# and those addresses were linked to. It is one page now: every old address is
# sent there for good, the pair kept in the query, where the page reads it to
# set its two pickers. One rule with a placeholder, not a line per pair, and
# above the last line, which would otherwise take them first.
/compare/:pair    /compare/?pair=:pair    301
/*    https://app.ekwo.ai/:splat    302
